# PROJECT: NEXT-GENERATION FREELANCING MARKETPLACE

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, Firebase engineer, database architect, and cybersecurity expert.

Build a complete, modern, responsive, production-oriented freelancing marketplace website inspired by Upwork, Fiverr, Freelancer, and Messenger.

The platform must connect freelancers (workers) with clients (people who need work done).

IMPORTANT: Do not build just a landing page or a static UI demo. Build a functional application with real authentication, database operations, job posting, freelancer profiles, messaging, file sharing, search, and all necessary pages.

Use Firebase for authentication and backend data storage.

Choose a professional brand name for the platform, and make the name, logo, colors, and branding easy to customize.

==================================================

1. TECHNOLOGY STACK
   ==================================================

Use:

* React with TypeScript.
* Vite for the frontend.
* Tailwind CSS for styling.
* Firebase Authentication for user authentication.
* Cloud Firestore for users, profiles, jobs, applications, conversations, messages, notifications, and reviews.
* Firebase Storage for profile pictures, portfolio images, videos, documents, and message attachments.
* Firebase Cloud Functions when server-side processing is necessary.
* Firebase App Check and appropriate security rules.
* A reliable date/time handling system.
* Responsive design for desktop, laptop, tablet, and mobile.

Use current, stable, compatible packages.

Organize the code into reusable components, pages, hooks, services, and types.

Never expose Firebase Admin credentials, private API keys, or service-account files in frontend code.

Do not use localStorage as the primary database for users, jobs, conversations, or messages.

